{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/260007-elemental-contract-ideas-for-shroudwrapped","id":260007,"title":"Elemental contract ideas for Shroudwrapped?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-18T13:16:07-07:00","id":260007,"title":"Elemental contract ideas for Shroudwrapped?","content":"My Storyteller and I are trying to figure out a balanced way to give my Shroudwrapped character a relevant elements contract, but we're having trouble finding something that's balanced. Here's the description for Shroudwrapped:<br /> <br /> &quot;Changelings who became the invisible agents of their Keeper's dominion, orchestrators of gravity and spacetime to mysteries dark matter and energy. The shroudwrapped have learned to reach out with the <b>Hand of the Cosmos</b>. Once per scene the Player may spend a point of Glamour to reach up to 2 yards per dot of Wyrd away, as if the space weren't there, provided there is nobody to witness the event. The blessing also grants the Changeling with an extra die on Larceny rolls.&quot;<br /> <br /> None of the traditional element contracts (for instance water, air, earth, metal, electricity etc) really fit. Gravity is a great idea, but it's difficult to fit into the parametres of the elements contracts. For example, Cloak of the Elements: protection from gravity? Sure, maybe to soften falls etc, but hard. And for &quot;Calling the Elements&quot; the player &quot;calls the associated element from a distant location. The changeling must either know the location or see the source of the element he is calling and the element must physically move toward the character in as natural manner as possible.&quot; The GM is concerned that the application of gravity is too difficult in some instances, and too powerful in others (i.e.,gravity is everywhere.)<br /> <br /> So has anyone played, or have ideas for a Shroudwrapped element, and how would that work? We've thought of gravity, radiation, dark matter... nothing really fits. Any creative ideas much appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3899,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3899-khakitsarina","user":"KhakiTsarina","date":". 09-18-2014, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3899-khakitsarina","name":"KhakiTsarina","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T21:12:53-07:00","id":260318,"title":"","content":"I don't know that there'll be a good option - Elements is generally intended to deal strictly with physical, generally tangible substances or processes. You could go with either light or darkness (or both, purchased individually) as similarly primal/energetic options, or air/wind if you want to focus on &quot;the stuff surrounding everyone.&quot; <br /> <br /> Or if you want to stick to the &quot;this is the guy who manipulated the cosmos&quot; theme, choose earth and say that he used his power to keep the planets spinning properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T10:02:43-07:00","id":260731,"title":"","content":"<i>suggestions, place emphasis on spacetime rather than gravity, as does the glamour ability:</i><br /> <br /> cloak of elements: protection from portals and traps that wisk you elsewhere<br /> <br /> armor of element's fury: your blows invoke shock from displacement, likewise blows against you bleed energy elsewhere and are lessened<br /> <br /> control elements: distort distances near you at will, slowing down opponents, or making them miss targets<br /> <br /> calling the element: create pockets of spacetime<br /> <br /> become the primal: ripple in spacetime, still somewhat visible and very hard to target, walk through small obstacles and thin walls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T10:58:59-07:00","id":260769,"title":"","content":"Those are both very good ideas, thanks! We were thinking of air contracts, but now I see that the earth contracts might make more sense. Also a good suggestion to tailor-make your own, although that still has some problems. For instance a lot of the elements contracts specify distance to or amount of the element present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3899-khakitsarina","name":"KhakiTsarina","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T01:38:14-07:00","id":261954,"title":"","content":"I've consulted some clever people and think I have a basis for gravity as an element. One guy said that the key to not having gravity be so overwhelming is that the changeling calls or borrows the gravitational pull of small solid object or distant celestial bodies - not earth itself. And that gravity would otherwise work much the same way that another intangible element would - much in the same way air would. You'd just have to modify the catches and modifiers a little. Add to that HobbitGuy1420's really good insight that gravity would basically also work much like Earth elemental, being able to move objects around. So I thought I'd take your advice. Using as much of the original contract text as possible, I tweaked it with a few explanations, borrowed catches from other contracts, and tried to make a balanced contract modification.<br /> <br /> Feedback and ideas appreciated. I think this might be something that a few other players could be interested in, too. There are still some kinks to work out, I think. For example, when you Become the Primal Foundation, would you be intangible like air or would you be capable of dealing damage? Or would it be something different entirely, like Arref's idea about being able to bend space-time and essentially teleport or walk through walls?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Gravity as an Elements Contract<br /> <br /> <br /> (note, unless otherwise specified, all the same failures, successes etc apply from the normal Element contracts)<br /> <br /> <b>Cloak of the Elements</b>: This clause protects the Elemental from the natural manifestations of any single element. The changeling can fall softly from a great height (within reason \u2013 a third-floor building, not a mountain) or things falling on top of him do less damage. In both cases he lands softly or the heavy thing bounces off or does less damage.<br /> <u>Catch: </u> is the same as for any element: The changeling bears some symbolic representation of the element in question, such as a souvenir T-shirt depicting a heavenly body.<br /> <br /> <b>Armor of the Elements Fury:</b> The character clothes himself in a frenzied and damaging manifestation of his chosen element, providing limited armor and damaging anyone who touches him. Contract sheathes the character in opposing forces of gravity which can pull apart whatever it touches. The character can control the extent of this manifestation, for instance, if limited to his hands, he can use them to attack others, or hover small objects over his palm.<br /> <u>Catch</u>: changeling touches both hands to solid ground as he invokes the contract.<br /> <br /> <b>Control elements:</b> Changeling can take control of the gravitational mass of a solid object or objects, causing the object(s) to move and act in the directed fashion, in the way a changeling attuned to non-solid elements could. They all have to be made of the same material, ie, a pile of gravel, or one single thing made of many materials, ie a radio.<br /> <u>Catch</u>: The changeling is calling the element solely to awe and impress viewers, perhaps as part of a performance.<br /> <br /> <b>Calling the Element</b>: The changeling borrows gravitational force from some celestial body from a distant location (ie it cannot be planet Earth). The changeling must either know the location or see the source of the body he is calling and the element must physically move toward the character in as natural manner as possible -- fire leaps, water splashes from a basin or falls as rain from the sky, gravity travels at the speed of light or through spacetime. When a gravity field is called, it creates a pocket of gravity that can either repel anything coming into it or pull everything towards it. Once the element is present, the changeling must then use the Control Element clause if he wishes to further control the element.<br /> <u>Catch</u>: the changeling is unhurried, calm and completely focused.<br /> <br /> <b>Become the Primal Foundation:</b> The changeling literally becomes a living manifestation of the Contract's associated element, The transformation takes only one turn. The character's clothing and small objects close to his skin, such as phones or wallets, blend into this elemental form.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The changeling becomes a living embodiment of the element -- in this case the character dissolves into the gravitational forces of milky way, a blur of stars and nebulae and black holes. The character retains all Mental and Social Attributes and Skills. Like characters who transform into air, water, fire or other formless elements, those aligned with gravity have no physical characteristics but triple the character's normal Speed. Gravity gives the changeling control over his own gravity, allowing him to hover and move in the same way air would. Elemental forms capable of damage either do lethal damage equal to half of the changeling's Wyrd (round up) or bashing damage equal to the changeling's Wyrd, depending upon the nature of the element. To attack in elemental form, the character makes a normal attack roll using either Brawl or Weaponry (the character's choice). Taking non-solid form makes the changeling largely immune from harm. If this element form is destroyed or seriously damaged (like being exposed to large magnetism, antimatter or significant sun spot activity, or a passing comet or meteor shower), the changeling automatically reverts to his normal form. Due to the shock, the changeling also loses two points of Willpower and cannot use this clause for one full day. Otherwise, the clause lasts for one scene, at which point the character must once again assume his normal form. The character can voluntarily resume his normal form, but doing so ends the Contract.<br /> <b>Catch:</b> The character must sit and meditate on the orbits of the galaxy for at least half an hour immediately before transforming.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3899-khakitsarina","name":"KhakiTsarina","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}